---
import PracticeLayout from '@/layouts/PracticeLayout.astro';

const SITE = 'https://mathpracticeonline.com';
const EFFECTIVE_DATE = 'August 25, 2026';
---

<PracticeLayout
  title="Privacy Policy — Math Practice Online"
  description="Learn how Math Practice Online handles browser-local progress and uses services for analytics, hosting, and advertising."
  canonical={`${SITE}/privacy`}
  breadcrumb={[{ label: 'Home', href: '/' }, { label: 'Privacy Policy' }]}
>
  <h1 slot="h1" class="text-3xl font-bold text-[#1E293B]">Privacy Policy</h1>
  <p slot="intro">
    Your privacy matters. This policy explains how Math Practice Online handles practice data and the
    third-party services used on the site.
  </p>

  <div slot="links" class="space-y-8 text-sm text-[#374151] leading-relaxed max-w-xl">

    <p class="text-xs text-[#6B7280]">Effective date: {EFFECTIVE_DATE}</p>

    <section>
      <h2 class="text-base font-semibold text-[#1E293B] mb-2">The short version</h2>
      <p>
        Math Practice Online does not require an account or ask you to provide a name, email address,
        password, student profile, or school or student identifier to use the practice tools. Scores,
        streaks, and other saved practice progress are stored locally in your browser. We also use
        third-party services for analytics, hosting, and advertising, as described below.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="text-base font-semibold text-[#1E293B] mb-2">Information you provide</h2>
      <p>
        The practice tools do not include account-registration or profile forms. You do not need to
        provide a name, email address, account credentials, student profile, or school or student
        identifier to practice.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="text-base font-semibold text-[#1E293B] mb-2">Practice progress in your browser</h2>
      <p>
        Scores, streaks, practice-session history, and applicable practice preferences are saved in
        your browser's <strong>localStorage</strong>. These Math Practice Online progress records do
        not require an account, are not uploaded to a Math Practice Online account, and are not
        synchronized between devices. You can remove them by clearing this site's data in your browser.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="text-base font-semibold text-[#1E293B] mb-2">Cookies</h2>
      <p>
        Third-party services used for analytics, advertising, and site operation may use cookies,
        browser storage, identifiers, or similar technologies where applicable. The technologies used
        can depend on the service, its configuration, your region, and applicable privacy requirements.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="text-base font-semibold text-[#1E293B] mb-2">Analytics</h2>
      <p>
        Math Practice Online uses Google Analytics 4 (GA4) to understand page and practice usage, site
        performance, and engagement so we can improve the site. Google Analytics may process technical
        information such as browser or device information, page and activity information, and cookies,
        identifiers, or similar technologies where applicable. You can opt out using the
        <a href="https://tools.google.com/dlpage/gaoptout" class="underline hover:text-[#4F46E5]" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Google Analytics Opt-out Browser Add-on</a>.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="text-base font-semibold text-[#1E293B] mb-2">Google AdSense and advertising</h2>
      <p>
        Math Practice Online includes Google AdSense advertising technology and may display advertising
        through Google AdSense to support free access to the site. Google and its advertising partners
        may process device or browser information, IP address and other request information, and cookies
        or other identifiers where applicable for ad delivery, measurement, security, fraud prevention,
        and related advertising operations. The processing that applies can depend on your region,
        Google settings, and applicable privacy requirements. The mathpracticeonline.com domain has been
        tagged with Google for child-directed treatment. Learn more about
        <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites" class="underline hover:text-[#4F46E5]" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">how Google uses information from sites or apps that use its services</a>.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="text-base font-semibold text-[#1E293B] mb-2">Children's privacy</h2>
      <p>
        Math Practice Online is designed for elementary-age students in K–5. Practice does not require
        an account, name, email address, password, or student profile. Saved practice progress remains in
        the browser and can be removed by clearing the site's browser data. The entire
        mathpracticeonline.com domain has been tagged with Google for child-directed treatment.
        Google Analytics, Google AdSense, and hosting and network services are described in the sections
        above and below.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="text-base font-semibold text-[#1E293B] mb-2">Third-party services</h2>
      <p>
        Google Analytics provides usage analytics, while Google AdSense provides advertising technology;
        each service is described separately above. The site also uses third-party hosting and network
        infrastructure. Those providers may process technical request information such as IP address,
        browser or device information, requested pages, and server-log information as part of normal site
        operation. Their processing is subject to their own privacy practices.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="text-base font-semibold text-[#1E293B] mb-2">Changes to this policy</h2>
      <p>
        If we make material changes to this privacy policy, we will update the effective date at the
        top of this page. We encourage you to review this page periodically.
      </p>
    </section>


  </div>
</PracticeLayout>
